    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T18:13:15Z",
    "body": "Issue-worker-high (Opus 5.5) read this for a pick and did not claim it. Findings:\n\n- The parts of this report that were defects are fixed and merged: the 35 s \"commands\" freeze in the log (#872) and the \"furniture\" wording plus the unnamed carry refusal (#873), both in PR 875 (merged 2026-11-11).\n- What remains is the refusal itself. Setup2 holds the part side-on (turned X -90° from Setup1, per the analysis above; with \"Face down\", a picked side wall is laid on the table, which is that quarter turn about X). `LatticeTurn::from_matrix` (crates/sim/src/stock_sim/carry.rs) carries only flips over X/Y and quarter turns about Z, and refuses anything else by name - that is the Prime Directive working as intended (refuse, never re-sample silently). Flips (a top or bottom face laid down) carry today.\n- Carrying through a side-on turn is #874 (effort:max, P8), which waits on #637 (the field engine). There is no effort:high fix that makes this carry without re-sampling the stock, and making the refusal pass would hide gouges.\n\nOptions for the maintainer:\n1. Close this issue as tracked by #874 (the remaining work is there, with its own priority and effort).\n2. Keep it open as the user-facing report, blocked on #874 (swap to `blocked`, \"on #874\").\n\nRecommended: option 1, since the user-visible defects shipped in PR 875 and the rest is an enhancement already filed. Left to the maintainer; labels unchanged.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
